No analytics or error monitoring currently deployed. Beta will be blind to usage and runtime errors.

Implementation:
1. Choose analytics tool (Alex to decide):
   - Option A: Plausible (privacy-first, GDPR-compliant, lightweight script)
   - Option B: umami (self-hosted alternative)
   - Option C: Firebase Analytics (already in deps, more invasive)
2. Add analytics script to apps/salon/index.html OR via Firebase SDK:
   - Track pageviews, /createur route visits
   - Track key events: account creation, article publish, puzzle completion
   - Do NOT track PII or message content
3. Choose error monitoring tool (Alex to decide):
   - Option A: Sentry (industry standard, generous free tier)
   - Option B: LogRocket (session replay + errors)
   - Option C: Custom Firestore error logging (minimal)
4. Integrate Sentry (recommended):
   - Install @sentry/react @sentry/vite-plugin
   - Initialize in src/main.tsx with DSN from Sentry project
   - Wrap app with Sentry.ErrorBoundary
   - Filter out permission-denied errors (expected for visitors)
5. Environment-gate both: only active in production, not dev

Pseudo-code (main.tsx with Sentry):
```typescript
import * as Sentry from '@sentry/react';

if (import.meta.env.PROD) {
  Sentry.init({
    dsn: import.meta.env.VITE_SENTRY_DSN,
    environment: 'production',
    beforeSend(event, hint) {
      // Filter expected permission errors from visitors
      if (hint.originalException?.code === 'permission-denied') return null;
      return event;
    },
  });
}

ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root')!).render(
  <Sentry.ErrorBoundary fallback={<ErrorFallback />}>
    <App />
  </Sentry.ErrorBoundary>
);
```

Chat has owner-delete and admin-delete but no user-initiated reporting for abuse. Moderation is reactive only.

Implementation:
1. Add "Report" button to each message in ChatRoom.tsx (show on hover, alongside existing delete button)
2. Button visible to all authenticated users (not just message owner)
3. On click, write to new Firestore collection /chatReports/{reportId}:
   - Fields: { reporterUid, reporterName, messageId, messageText, messageAuthorUid, room, reportedAt, status: 'pending' }
4. Add Firestore rule for /chatReports:
   - allow create: if request.auth != null && request.resource.data.status == 'pending'
   - allow read, update: if isAdmin()
5. Admin CRM: add "Reports" tab to read and triage reports (mark as reviewed/actioned/dismissed)
6. UI feedback: show toast "Message reported" after successful write
7. Rate-limit: client-side check prevents same user reporting same message twice (store in localStorage)

Pseudo-code (ChatRoom.tsx):
```typescript
const reportMessage = async (msg: ChatMessage) => {
  if (!currentUser) return;
  const reportKey = `reported-${msg.id}`;
  if (localStorage.getItem(reportKey)) {
    alert(t('Already reported', 'Déjà signalé'));
    return;
  }

  const db = studioDb();
  if (!db) return;

  await addDoc(collection(db, 'chatReports'), {
    reporterUid: currentUser.uid,
    reporterName: displayName || currentUser.displayName,
    messageId: msg.id,
    messageText: msg.text,
    messageAuthorUid: msg.uid,
    room: activeRoom,
    reportedAt: serverTimestamp(),
    status: 'pending',
  });

  localStorage.setItem(reportKey, 'true');
  showToast(t('Message reported', 'Message signalé'));
};
```

Firestore rules addition:
```
match /chatReports/{reportId} {
  allow create: if request.auth != null
                && request.resource.data.status == 'pending'
                && request.resource.data.reporterUid == request.auth.uid;
  allow read, update, delete: if isAdmin();
}
```

Skin purchases currently simulated with honest confirm dialog. Real Stripe integration is an ALEX DECISION (during or after beta).

Implementation (if approved):
1. Install @stripe/stripe-js and Stripe backend SDK
2. Create Cloud Function createCheckoutSession:
   - Input: { skinId, priceUSD, uid }
   - Creates Stripe checkout session with line item for skin
   - Returns session URL
3. Update skin purchase UI (likely in ArtistHub or skins marketplace):
   - On "Buy Skin" click, call createCheckoutSession
   - Redirect user to Stripe-hosted checkout (session.url)
4. Create webhook handler fulfillCheckout:
   - Listens for checkout.session.completed event from Stripe
   - Writes purchased skin to members/{uid}/artistProfile/purchasedSkins
   - Deducts coins from user balance if using hybrid coin+USD model
5. Add Stripe publishable key to environment (VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY)
6. Firestore rules: ensure purchasedSkins can only be written by Cloud Function (admin SDK)
7. Test mode: use Stripe test keys and test card 4242 4242 4242 4242

Pseudo-code (Cloud Function):
```typescript
import Stripe from 'stripe';
const stripe = new Stripe(process.env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY);

export const createCheckoutSession = onCall(async (request) => {
  const { skinId, priceUSD } = request.data;
  const uid = request.auth?.uid;
  if (!uid) throw new Error('Not authenticated');

  const session = await stripe.checkout.sessions.create({
    payment_method_types: ['card'],
    line_items: [{
      price_data: {
        currency: 'usd',
        product_data: { name: `Skin: ${skinId}` },
        unit_amount: priceUSD * 100, // cents
      },
      quantity: 1,
    }],
    mode: 'payment',
    success_url: `https://inconnus-salon.web.app/createur?purchase=success`,
    cancel_url: `https://inconnus-salon.web.app/createur?purchase=cancel`,
    metadata: { uid, skinId },
  });

  return { url: session.url };
});

export const fulfillCheckout = onRequest(async (req, res) => {
  const sig = req.headers['stripe-signature'];
  const event = stripe.webhooks.constructEvent(req.rawBody, sig, process.env.STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET);

  if (event.type === 'checkout.session.completed') {
    const session = event.data.object;
    const { uid, skinId } = session.metadata;

    await db.doc(`members/${uid}/artistProfile/purchasedSkins`).set(
      { [skinId]: { purchasedAt: FieldValue.serverTimestamp(), priceUSD: session.amount_total / 100 } },
      { merge: true }
    );
  }

  res.json({ received: true });
});
```
